 "tier1Summary": "[[p:Donald Trump]] reached Shenzhen for [[e:APEC China 2026]], where [[p:Xi Jinping]] met him at the plane. Their summit and the first US–China–Russia leaders' meeting with [[p:Vladimir Putin]] follow on 19 Nov. Washington also closed a loophole letting Chinese firms rent US AI chips abroad. In Manila the Quad agreed joint maritime surveillance, while ASEAN and China again missed a South China Sea code.\n\nThree capitals were shaken. Indonesia's vice president [[p:Gibran Rakabuming Raka]] resigned as a Jokowi-era police chief faces treason charges. Mongolia's president said he will quit over bribery claims. Malaysia's ruling bloc was routed in Melaka.\n\nElsewhere: an Indian sailor is missing after a Hormuz tanker attack, the [[p:Houthis]] are about 60 km from Aden, and Africa CDC says Congo's Ebola outbreak is out of control.",
